{"meta":{"ticker":"GARP","as_of_date":"2026-09-21","performance_as_of":"2026-08-31","generated_at":"2026-09-22 07:37:57"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"GARP","fund_name":"iShares MSCI USA Quality GARP ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Growth","issuer":"BlackRock","index_name":"MSCI USA Quality GARP Select Index","region":"North America","exchange":"BATS","expense_ratio":0.0015,"aum":3165130177,"holdings_count":134,"inception_date":"2020-06-14","overall_score":7.83811207964602,"overall_rank":203,"sector_diversification_score":4.88200437731363},"description":{"tsi_description":"GARP is a large-cap growth ETF that tracks the MSCI USA Quality GARP Select Index and emphasizes companies with strong growth characteristics alongside reasonable valuations and quality metrics. The strategy combines growth, value, and quality screens within the MSCI USA Index universe, with growth scores driving security selection and value and quality scores influencing portfolio weights. Compared to many concentrated mega-cap growth ETFs, GARP maintains broader sector exposure and lower concentration in the largest technology companies. The fund also incorporates buffer rules and quarterly rebalancing to help manage portfolio turnover over time. Overall, GARP offers a structured growth-at-a-reasonable-price approach through a transparent multi-factor indexing framework.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the MSCI USA Quality GARP Select Index.","Starts with companies in the MSCI USA Index.","Covers approximately 50% of the weight of the parent index.","Calculates growth scores using long-term and short-term estimated earnings growth, internal growth rate, long-term earnings growth trends, and historical sales growth trends.","Calculates value scores using forward price-to-earnings, enterprise value-to-operating cash flow, and price-to-book ratios, with sector-specific exceptions.","Calculates quality scores using return on equity, debt-to-